      "note": "Voted aye (66-47). The fifth edition of the bill text keeps photo ID for in-person voting and for absentee ballots, lets a voter without photo ID cast a provisional ballot and bring ID to the county board afterward, and extends to five business days the time to show ID when ID numbers do not match. It also adds a rule that a driver-license or ID-card registration worker must ask whether the applicant is a citizen and proceed only if the applicant says yes. Bill text: https://www.ncleg.gov/Sessions/2025/Bills/House/PDF/H958v5.pdf",
